WEBVTT

00:04.790 --> 00:06.210
Eiko told me.

00:07.580 --> 00:08.670
About your hand.

00:09.130 --> 00:11.500
It looks like hair, right?

00:11.790 --> 00:14.130
It's not, though. They're actually...

00:14.830 --> 00:16.000
...his nerves.

00:16.790 --> 00:17.880
Something's off.

00:19.080 --> 00:20.830
This is someone's left hand.

00:21.210 --> 00:23.880
Keitaro's curse is on his right hand.

00:24.630 --> 00:27.960
Good eye, Yayoi-chan.
I'm not surprised you figured it out.

00:29.710 --> 00:31.630
You're right. It's not his hand.

00:33.920 --> 00:35.580
It's mine.

00:42.170 --> 00:45.830
I was hit by the curse in the summer of ninth grade.

00:46.830 --> 00:48.630
And Eiko got tangled up in it, to.

00:49.580 --> 00:52.710
If we kill the spirit behind the curse, it'll go away.

00:54.210 --> 00:56.880
Both of you will be free.

00:58.960 --> 01:00.210
I can...

01:01.290 --> 01:02.500
...save Eiko?

01:04.580 --> 01:07.080
Can I have some time to think?

01:07.460 --> 01:08.330
Don't worry.

01:09.420 --> 01:13.750
If anyone thinks you're some creep trying to get to me,
I'll tell them you're my tutor.

01:13.750 --> 01:14.420
What?

01:14.920 --> 01:17.130
And that you're definitely not trying to kidnap me.

01:17.130 --> 01:18.880
That's not what I'm worried about!

01:20.210 --> 01:21.830
It's something a lot more serious.

01:22.750 --> 01:24.250
I want to help Eiko.

01:25.210 --> 01:30.330
She's the person who helped me stop hiding
in my room and get back to the real world.

01:31.210 --> 01:36.130
But taking Yayoi up on her offer
means turning my back on that world...

01:37.290 --> 01:39.040
and diving deeper into the occult.

01:40.630 --> 01:46.290
I can either keep trying to live a normal life,
far from the supernatural, or...

01:47.290 --> 01:50.920
I can purposely immerse myself in it to save Eiko.

01:53.420 --> 01:54.420
What do I choose?

03:28.130 --> 03:31.250
Okay, which one should I wear, Kei-kun?

03:31.540 --> 03:35.000
You'll look good in both!
We gotta go, we're gonna miss the train!

03:37.130 --> 03:38.710
Fine, then, we'll just drive!

03:38.830 --> 03:44.290
Wait, drive to school? I'm pretty sure campus
doesn't allow us to commute by car...

03:44.290 --> 03:45.210
Who cares?!

03:45.540 --> 03:48.170
I'll take the toll road
so we get there in time! Just pick one!

03:49.500 --> 03:53.630
I've always wanted to make the drive to school instead!

03:53.630 --> 03:55.460
H-hope we don't get in trouble...

03:56.250 --> 03:57.750
Keitaro, you scaredy-cat.

03:58.330 --> 03:59.460
Yayoi-chan?!

03:59.460 --> 04:00.170
'Sup?

04:00.460 --> 04:02.920
What are you doing here? Don't you have school?!

04:02.920 --> 04:06.630
We're still on spring break.
I'm gonna come tour campus with you.

04:06.880 --> 04:09.750
Look at you, getting a head start, Yayoi-chan!

04:09.830 --> 04:12.130
C-can we really just bring her with us?

04:12.540 --> 04:16.250
Today's just orientation and demo classes, anyway.
I don't see why not!

04:19.830 --> 04:20.710
I'm so excited!

04:21.170 --> 04:21.790
Huh?

04:23.170 --> 04:23.750
Yeah.

04:26.670 --> 04:30.080
Our lives as college students finally start today.

04:36.830 --> 04:39.540
Are you the esteemed Eiko Hozuki?!

04:40.080 --> 04:42.580
Wait, what?!

04:42.580 --> 04:43.920
I-it really is you!

04:43.920 --> 04:47.500
You must join our Informatics Team, we beseech you!

04:48.000 --> 04:51.580
I didn't know there were so many of your types around.
You know these guys?

04:51.880 --> 04:55.330
Not at all. Wait, you really think I'm like these guys?

04:55.960 --> 04:59.540
You were chosen to represent Japan
in the International Olympiad in Informatics!

04:59.540 --> 05:04.130
And you're already in fourth-year classes!
You have to pass an interview to get into those!

05:04.330 --> 05:06.290
What a brilliant mind you must possess!

05:06.290 --> 05:07.290
Wait, really?!

05:07.540 --> 05:08.630
That's incredible!

05:08.630 --> 05:09.710
We have to connect!

05:10.540 --> 05:12.580
I didn't know Eiko was a big deal.

05:12.580 --> 05:15.420
Me neither. You couldn't tell from how she acts.

05:16.080 --> 05:17.420
Say "logarithm"!

05:16.210 --> 05:18.790
<b>Logarithm~</b>

05:17.420 --> 05:18.630
Extroverts are crazy!

05:19.290 --> 05:22.040
What's he doing with that little girl?

05:19.500 --> 05:22.040
Meanwhile, everyone thinks I'm some sort of creep.

05:22.380 --> 05:24.210
No respect for the highest scorer
on the entrance exam, huh?

05:24.750 --> 05:28.790
I-I'm gonna break out of my shell
and be a normal member of society!

05:29.250 --> 05:30.750
And it's thanks to her...

05:31.830 --> 05:36.710
Eiko is always there for me,
even though she was hit by the same curse.

05:38.080 --> 05:41.250
I thought she'd push me away for getting her hurt,

05:41.630 --> 05:45.580
but she told me not to worry about it
and stayed by my side anyway,

05:46.500 --> 05:50.460
while I just sat there and wallowed in my guilt.

05:51.210 --> 05:54.420
But maybe she really didn't have any hard feelings
about what happened.

05:55.420 --> 05:59.920
Maybe I'm a terrible person for assuming she did...

06:00.080 --> 06:02.130
Kei-kun!

06:02.630 --> 06:08.000
I got some flyers for some easy-peasy classes.
Let's go register for classes together!

06:08.880 --> 06:10.580
What about your new friends?

06:10.580 --> 06:14.250
It's fine! I got their numbers,
so we're gonna hang out later.

06:14.710 --> 06:16.460
Bye!

06:17.040 --> 06:19.210
And I'm not going to join their team.

06:19.210 --> 06:20.710
Really? You sure?

06:20.920 --> 06:23.040
I'm majoring in folklore now.

06:24.130 --> 06:29.790
Besides, I'd much rather have fun
taking classes with you, Kei-kun!

06:33.880 --> 06:35.460
Th-thanks...

06:35.460 --> 06:36.790
Don't mention it!

06:37.500 --> 06:39.210
College life sure seems fun.

06:43.130 --> 06:44.580
What does "register" mean?

06:44.830 --> 06:47.040
It means signing up for classes.

06:47.330 --> 06:49.290
In college, we get to pick which ones we take.

06:49.290 --> 06:50.130
Cool.

06:50.250 --> 06:52.250
See any interesting classes we could take?

06:54.040 --> 06:55.040
<b>URBAN LEGENDS:</b>

06:54.040 --> 06:55.040
<b>SCARY STORIES</b>

06:56.920 --> 06:59.420
Y-you want to take that one?

06:59.420 --> 07:01.500
O-of course not!

07:02.630 --> 07:04.210
You won't catch me dead in that class.

07:04.830 --> 07:06.920
I know...

07:08.630 --> 07:10.000
I didn't think she'd get that upset!

07:10.830 --> 07:14.670
Ever since Eiko was little, she's loved scary stories.

07:15.040 --> 07:18.210
She doesn't bring it up much in front of me now, though.

07:18.880 --> 07:21.130
She must still feel the same about them now...

07:22.210 --> 07:24.920
I really don't want to have to go to that class, but...

07:25.210 --> 07:25.960
<b>URBAN LEGENDS</b>

07:25.960 --> 07:26.710
<b>SCARY STORIES</b>

07:37.210 --> 07:39.080
I-I'll go to the demo...

07:39.830 --> 07:40.710
Great!

07:41.130 --> 07:48.580
I'm good at all sorts of sciences, so there's something
so exciting about unexplainable happenings!

07:48.580 --> 07:49.710
I get it.

07:49.880 --> 07:50.830
I don't.

07:51.540 --> 07:55.080
Is it the same excitement you get
from hearing a fun story about something?

07:55.630 --> 07:59.420
<b>MONDAY 3RD PERIOD</b>

07:55.630 --> 07:59.420
<b>URBAN LEGENDS</b>

07:56.920 --> 07:59.080
Welcome, horror enthusiasts.

07:59.630 --> 08:05.000
In my class, you'll be introduced
to terrifying mysteries and experience true fear.

08:05.920 --> 08:07.920
Stay seated, if you dare.

08:08.080 --> 08:10.460
I'm experiencing true fear already!

08:10.710 --> 08:14.670
Today, we have this VHS tape.
A video, as you kids would say.

08:15.040 --> 08:18.790
Recorded on it is an art major's graduation project.

08:18.790 --> 08:21.790
His topic? Suicide.

08:23.210 --> 08:27.040
Overwhelmed by the stress
to complete his graduation project,

08:27.130 --> 08:33.130
the student fell into a state of psychosis and decided
to film his self-immolation, then turned it into his advisor.

08:33.420 --> 08:37.420
"Well, how'd he do that
when he was dead?" I hear you wondering.

08:37.420 --> 08:39.670
But there's something more sinister than that:

08:40.880 --> 08:44.880
Whoever watches this video will suddenly find
that they have become the artist,

08:46.170 --> 08:50.080
and die within flame of their own making...
Or so the story goes.

08:50.250 --> 08:52.750
CAN I LEAVE? CAN I LEAVE? CAN I LEAVE?!

08:52.170 --> 08:53.830
Shall we see if the story's true?

09:44.290 --> 09:45.500
Wait, did it just...?

09:45.500 --> 09:46.540
It's someone else.

09:49.330 --> 09:51.000
Kei-kun?

10:13.790 --> 10:19.210
H-how?! I checked the video before class,
and that wasn't on it!

10:19.380 --> 10:21.460
I need to go check with a colleague! Stay here!

10:21.880 --> 10:23.830
This class is sus as hell.

10:23.830 --> 10:24.960
Yeah, let's get outta here.

10:39.250 --> 10:43.000
I put our nails inside these plushies.

10:44.040 --> 10:46.750
It's probably protecting you right now.

10:47.670 --> 10:54.210
We need to kill the spirit or get rid of the curse
before it burns through my plushies...

10:57.380 --> 10:59.290
...or Keitaro's gonna die a fiery death.

11:06.630 --> 11:08.290
Y..Yayoi-chan?!

11:08.540 --> 11:09.500
What are you doing?

11:15.420 --> 11:16.380
Caught it.

11:17.630 --> 11:19.920
H-how'd you do that?

11:20.380 --> 11:24.540
I used salt to force it out of the tape
and caught it with a doll it can possess.

11:25.580 --> 11:29.630
It has to be pretty powerful if it can burn my plushies.

11:30.830 --> 11:34.960
We can't kill it now, so we'll have to stop the curse.

11:36.080 --> 11:36.920
What're you doing there?

11:37.130 --> 11:42.170
The curse makes it so whoever watches the video
becomes the victim dying in it.

11:42.670 --> 11:51.290
So, if we force the spirit itself to watch the video, it'll be
forced to dispel the curse before it becomes the victim.

11:52.580 --> 11:53.290
I think.

11:53.880 --> 11:54.960
You think...?

11:59.170 --> 12:01.790
So... that solves that, then?

12:02.210 --> 12:03.420
That easily?

12:03.830 --> 12:08.130
O-oh, wow. Guess I didn't need
to be that scared after all.

12:17.500 --> 12:18.330
Kei-kun!

12:24.920 --> 12:28.580
I-it's not over... It's still here!

12:48.130 --> 12:50.500
<b>MONDAY 3RD PERIOD</b>

12:48.130 --> 12:50.500
<b>URBAN LEGENDS</b>

12:49.380 --> 12:54.000
The spirit probably feels threatened
by the setup in the box,

12:54.290 --> 12:58.420
and it couldn't hurt you,
so it went after your clothes instead.

12:59.330 --> 13:00.750
We'll need more to stop it.

13:01.830 --> 13:03.540
Eiko, I need a favor.

13:03.670 --> 13:04.500
Huh?

13:04.750 --> 13:08.420
I've got something in my room that'll do it.
Drive me home.

13:08.420 --> 13:09.540
You want to get in a car?!

13:10.080 --> 13:13.920
If it lights stuff on fire,
and the gas tank explodes, then you'll die!

13:13.920 --> 13:14.710
Keitaro.

13:15.830 --> 13:18.250
Keeping it here on campus is too dangerous.

13:18.250 --> 13:23.380
And if we don't drive, we have to carry it
through town, or on public transit.

13:24.630 --> 13:31.000
We need to pick the option that will get us there
the fastest, with minimal risk to human casualties.

13:31.540 --> 13:34.670
If we bring that thing home,
you can save Kei-kun from its curse?

13:35.790 --> 13:36.790
Without a doubt.

13:37.330 --> 13:39.250
Okay, then let me drive her back-

13:39.250 --> 13:40.210
No!

13:41.500 --> 13:43.250
I'll take care of it myself.

13:44.500 --> 13:50.250
I don't want anyone else I love to get hurt. Not again.

13:52.210 --> 13:53.460
Kei-kun...

13:54.830 --> 13:58.130
The professor said he watched it before,
but didn’t get cursed.

13:58.670 --> 14:02.830
That means not everyone who watches it gets cursed.

14:04.080 --> 14:07.080
I can't guarantee this setup will work
to transfer the curse.

14:08.580 --> 14:09.380
Keitaro?

14:15.040 --> 14:15.960
Eiko?

14:16.210 --> 14:20.210
Hey, Kei-kun. We've known each other forever, right?

14:21.500 --> 14:26.960
I've noticed something you always do for me,
ever since we were kids.

14:29.210 --> 14:30.000
Eiko.

14:31.380 --> 14:34.330
Don't go near that pole, okay?

14:34.830 --> 14:35.540
Huh?

14:37.580 --> 14:42.790
Just after you warned me about it,
a horrible accident happened right there.

14:44.500 --> 14:45.830
I'm glad you're okay.

14:48.380 --> 14:53.540
In my world there was me and my good grades,
the popular kids in school, grown-ups,

14:53.830 --> 14:58.250
and standing apart from them all was you
and the mysterious power you possessed.

14:59.210 --> 15:05.130
And you used your spiritual sensitivity to protect me
without asking anything in return.

15:05.960 --> 15:08.290
Then there's what happened to my hand.

15:10.130 --> 15:15.080
You keep blaming yourself for "hurting" me,
but that's not what happened.

15:15.830 --> 15:18.500
I made you come with me on that test of courage,

15:18.750 --> 15:22.580
and you protected me from something scary,
which cursed you.

15:23.500 --> 15:31.750
Sure, it ended up cursing me, too, but if you
hadn't protected me, I might not be here right now.

15:33.080 --> 15:36.920
I want to pay you back
for all the times you've protected me.

15:38.540 --> 15:42.750
You've always been there for me.
I want to be there for you, too.

15:46.460 --> 15:51.080
She said as much back then, too.
Those words pulled me from the abyss.

15:52.380 --> 15:56.830
She's cared about me this whole time.
How the hell did I not see it?

15:59.130 --> 16:01.710
Eiko, Yayoi-chan...

16:03.830 --> 16:05.500
Would you please help me?

16:10.330 --> 16:12.040
It's not fair, Keitaro.

16:12.630 --> 16:14.790
I wanna get cursed by spirits, too!

16:14.790 --> 16:16.880
We were having a moment here!

16:17.290 --> 16:18.790
A-ahem!

16:18.960 --> 16:21.880
I-it sounds like we're all in agreement now, yeah?

16:22.080 --> 16:22.750
Yup.

16:23.040 --> 16:23.880
Okay, then.

16:24.290 --> 16:26.540
I've got a plan.

16:28.210 --> 16:29.580
WHAT KIND OF PLAN IS THIS?!

16:29.790 --> 16:33.710
A plan where you can put the only
burnable part of you out the window!

16:33.710 --> 16:34.790
Fun!

16:34.790 --> 16:36.210
I'M NOT HAVING FUN!

16:36.380 --> 16:40.670
Why do I have this on my arm?!
Wouldn't it be better if I was totally naked?

16:40.830 --> 16:44.420
If you were, then it might try
to light the car or something else on fire.

16:44.710 --> 16:49.880
The curse should transfer over
after it's watched the full video.

16:50.540 --> 16:57.080
So if we can make the spirit watch the full video
while it's trapped in there, we win.

16:57.750 --> 17:00.130
It's gonna try to fight back, though.

17:02.420 --> 17:09.040
It's not doing anything now, but as soon
as we start driving, I'm gonna press play.

17:09.830 --> 17:14.250
Then it'll probably light some fires trying to get free.

17:14.500 --> 17:18.880
So you want me to put the fire out
by putting my arm out the car window?

17:19.290 --> 17:20.540
Will that really work?

17:20.920 --> 17:25.880
It will. You just need to hang in there
until the video plays through to the end.

17:26.790 --> 17:31.250
And Eiko needs to keep driving fast enough
to put out the fire with the rushing outside air.

17:32.630 --> 17:34.250
Brace yourself, Keitaro.

17:34.630 --> 17:36.460
Ugh, yeah, whatever!

17:36.880 --> 17:38.500
Let's ghoooo...

17:38.500 --> 17:39.580
...ooost!

17:40.880 --> 17:42.040
Pressing play.

17:47.420 --> 17:48.080
Here it comes!

17:58.330 --> 17:59.790
Eiko, gun it!

17:59.790 --> 18:00.580
You got it!

18:11.630 --> 18:12.830
Faster, Eiko!

18:12.960 --> 18:13.580
Okay!

18:22.630 --> 18:25.500
It turned the light red to try to kill us...

18:29.210 --> 18:32.670
That must be its last resort. It's gotta be close.

18:33.420 --> 18:35.170
Don't stop! Speed up!

18:54.210 --> 18:56.080
Th-that was close...

18:56.080 --> 18:58.170
D-did we do it?

19:03.460 --> 19:07.460
Thank... Thank God...

19:09.710 --> 19:12.330
Welcome to my room.

19:13.130 --> 19:14.710
Have fun, you guys.

19:25.580 --> 19:29.670
Sorry, Kei-kun. If I hadn't invited you
to that creepy class...

19:30.790 --> 19:35.250
Hey, it was my fault you had to help with that scary stuff,
and come to the hospital, too.

19:35.500 --> 19:39.580
Thank you, seriously. For everything.

19:39.920 --> 19:42.130
You're so sweet, Kei-kun.

19:42.580 --> 19:45.750
Oh, when you were seeing the doctor,

19:46.000 --> 19:48.580
Yayoi-chan called and said she found out
where the cursed video came from.

19:48.830 --> 19:50.830
She did? Who'd she talk to.

19:51.460 --> 19:54.130
The carcass of the spirit from the video.

19:54.130 --> 19:55.960
Y..Yayoi-chan...

19:56.500 --> 20:00.750
Someone forced them to kill themselves
and recorded the whole thing.

20:02.710 --> 20:05.170
They were being bullied.

20:07.000 --> 20:10.630
I mean, it's way worse than bullying. They murdered him.

20:12.250 --> 20:17.250
They picked on him to help "blow off stress,"
and the bullying just kept escalating,

20:18.170 --> 20:20.750
to the point where they were
even messing with his family.

20:22.500 --> 20:27.330
Then the story got so twisted that they blamed
the horrified victim for the curse...

20:28.880 --> 20:31.460
The curse started with the victimized art student,

20:31.830 --> 20:36.040
who sought out his bully and killed them
to sate his venegeance and finally rest.

20:36.920 --> 20:42.080
But the bully killed by the curse was furious,
and lingered behind to keep it going.

20:42.960 --> 20:45.710
The first victim started the curse
under desperate circumstances.

20:45.880 --> 20:48.540
This spirit, though, shouldn't be shown any mercy.

20:48.880 --> 20:54.500
She said not to worry, that she "taught it a lesson."
Wonder what that means...

20:56.960 --> 20:59.250
People really "bully" each other like that?

20:59.920 --> 21:03.170
Making friends is a lot harder than it sounds...

21:04.290 --> 21:09.460
Do I really have what it takes
to avoid something like that and make real friends?

21:10.580 --> 21:15.790
Can I stay friends with Eiko
and graduate with her smiling by my side?

21:16.170 --> 21:19.830
I'm just really glad you're okay, Kei-kun.

21:21.540 --> 21:25.420
I can't wait to see what kind of fun
we're gonna have in college together!

21:28.750 --> 21:35.210
At the very least, I can make sure I keep caring for her
as much as I always have.

21:36.080 --> 21:38.080
Yeah, same here.

21:41.710 --> 21:43.040
I'm home!

21:53.710 --> 21:57.040
For a second, I was really scared
he wasn't gonna make it.

21:59.830 --> 22:01.040
I'm sorry.

22:02.420 --> 22:07.040
I never, ever want you to get hurt, but...

22:07.540 --> 22:11.540
...but I can't help how much I love spooky stuff.

22:12.920 --> 22:14.000
And now...

22:14.750 --> 22:18.920
I don't want anyone else I love to get hurt. Not again.

22:21.460 --> 22:26.130
The closer I get to the darkness,
the harder you try to protect me from it.

22:26.960 --> 22:32.130
Then I get to have the two things I love:
spooky stuff AND you. I just can't stop.

22:33.000 --> 22:35.750
Not when I can feel how much you love me.

22:37.960 --> 22:38.960
Kei-kun...

22:40.420 --> 22:43.830
I'm so addicted to you.

22:47.670 --> 22:54.040
We made it through today, so I get to be with you
tomorrow, and the day after that, and forever and ever!

22:57.210 --> 23:00.960
Let's go catch some scary spirits
and get them to kill some really bad ones.

23:02.290 --> 23:03.130
Together.

23:05.500 --> 23:08.460
Either I lift the curse, or choose not to...

23:10.040 --> 23:13.960
Which one would be better for Eiko?

23:22.460 --> 23:28.250
Keitaro once shut himself in his room,
isolating himself from all others.

23:29.290 --> 23:31.460
Now, he hopes to find companionship again,

23:32.130 --> 23:39.710
but when he gets the courage to socialize, will he find
what he's looking for, or something more sinister?
